```plaintext
2result.sql
```

Reason:  
• It works at the location / purchase‑lot level by joining each pick line to the corresponding inventory row, then keeps only the earliest‑purchase / smallest‑quantity lot for every location, so the FIFO rule is honoured.  
• The picked quantity for every pick line is clipped to the overlap with that lot’s available stock ( MIN(pl.qty, stock_qty) ), giving the correct “pick‑percentage” per line before averaging.  
• It finally averages those percentages per product name and orders the output alphabetically, exactly matching the requirement.  

The other scripts fail key points:  
– 0result.sql ignores inventory lots altogether (no FIFO, uses total stock).  
– 1result.sql treats already‑picked quantity as the demand and compares it to total stock, again skipping FIFO and the required overlap logic.